// =====================================================================
// Rule 6: Privilege Escalation via Role Assignment
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
// Purpose: Detects a new role being granted (roleAssignments/write) -
// how an attacker who has already gotten in expands permissions for
// a more durable foothold.
//
// Data source : AzureActivity_CL
// Severity    : High
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1098 - Account Manipulation (Privilege Escalation)
// Schedule    : Daily
//
// Entity mapping:
//   Account -> FullName -> Caller
//   IP      -> Address  -> IP
//
// NOTE ON TESTING: the live Azure Activity connector can lag behind a
// real role assignment (ingestion latency, not a bug). If the rule
// doesn't fire against a role change you just made, supplement a
// confirmed event with scripts/inject-test-scenarios.ps1
// (-Scenario PrivilegeEscalation) rather than waiting indefinitely.
// =====================================================================

AzureActivity_CL
| where OperationNameValue_s has "roleAssignments/write"
| extend Caller = Caller_s, IP = CallerIPAddress
| project TimeGenerated, Caller, IP
